<title>UK: Union backs block on Bass /Carlberg deal.</title>
<headline>Union backs block on Bass /Carlberg deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Transport and General Workers Union (T&amp;G) said on Friday it backed the UK government's decision to block the proposed merger between brewing giant Bass Plc and Carlsberg-Tetley.</p>
<p>The union said it had lobbied the Monopolies and Mergers Commission on the issue and estimated that had the deal been cleared, two thousand jobs would have been lost.</p>
<p>The T&amp;G said it conceded there was a danger of job cuts within Carlsberg-Tetley but &quot;this is likely to be substantially less than if the merger was allowed to go ahead&quot;, a union statement said.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 5427717.</p>
